Whispers of the Wind

The wind hums soft, a lullaby,
Beneath the painted evening sky.
It weaves through trees, a fleeting ghost,
A whispered song we love the most.

It dances over rolling hills,
Through golden fields, so calm, so still.
It tells of tales from far and wide,
Of ocean waves and shifting tides.

So listen close, just pause and hear,
The wind has secrets, bright and clear.
It sings of dreams yet left untold,
A story whispered, brave and bold.

